  A: [{
    k: 'Hikoya', t: 'A Week Full of Phrasal Verbs', s: 'Sardor haftasi: rejalar barbod bo‘ldi, lekin kutilmagan voqealar ham bo‘ldi',
    p: [
      ['Sardor was always busy. Every evening he would [wind down|wind down] with music, but often he would [nod off|nod off] on the sofa. On Monday he had to [fill in|fill in] a long form and [back up|back up] his files. His boss had [put off|put off] the meeting twice. Sardor was not sure he could [keep up with|keep up with] everything. “I have to [scale back on|scale back on] coffee,” he thought, “and [stick to|stick to] my plan.”',
       'Sardor doim band edi. Har kuni kechqurun musiqa bilan xotirjam bo‘lar, lekin tez-tez divanda mudrab qolardi. Dushanba kuni u uzun anketani to‘ldirishi va fayllarini zaxiralashi kerak edi. Boshlig‘i yig‘ilishni ikki marta kechiktirgan edi. Sardor hamma narsaga ulgurishiga ishonchi komil emas edi. «Kofeni kamaytirishim kerak, — deb o‘yladi u, — va rejaga amal qilishim kerak.»'],
      ['On Tuesday his friend asked him to [drop by|drop by] for dinner, but Sardor [turned down|turn down] the invitation. His friend was [mixing up|mix up] the dates, and the plan [fell through|fall through]. On Wednesday a colleague didn’t [turn up|turn up] to work, so Sardor had to [deal with|deal with] two projects. He [hung up|hang up] angrily after a long call. “I [count on|count on] people, and they let me down,” he said. He wanted to [get over|get over] this stress.',
       'Seshanba kuni do‘sti uni kechki ovqatga kirib o‘tishga chaqirdi, lekin Sardor taklifni rad etdi. Do‘sti sanalarni adashtirgan edi va reja barbod bo‘ldi. Chorshanba kuni hamkasbi ishga kelmadi, shuning uchun Sardor ikkita loyiha bilan shug‘ullanishi kerak edi. U uzun suhbatdan keyin jahl bilan trubkani qo‘ydi. «Men odamlarga tayanaman, ular esa meni xafa qiladi», dedi u. U bu stressni unutmoqchi edi.'],
      ['On Thursday he [ran into|run into] his old teacher, whom he always [looked up to|look up to]. The teacher said, “You [take after|take after] your father — always so responsible.” They chatted, and Sardor decided to [carry out|carry out] his dream: to [set up|set up] a small company. He had [gone through|go through] hard times before, so he knew he could [make up for|make up for] the lost time. “I will [look into|look into] it,” he promised, and started to [clear out|clear out] his flat to find the money.',
       'Payshanba kuni u eski ustoziga duch keldi, uni doim hurmat qilardi. Ustoz dedi: «Sen otangga o‘xshaysan — doim mas’uliyatli.» Ular suhbatlashdi va Sardor orzusini amalga oshirishga — kichik kompaniya tashkil etishga qaror qildi. U oldin ham qiyin vaqtlarni boshdan kechirgan edi, shuning uchun yo‘qotilgan vaqtning o‘rnini qoplashiga ishondi. «Buni tekshirib ko‘raman», deb va’da berdi u va pul topish uchun kvartirasini tozalay boshladi.'],
      ['On Friday he had to [throw away|throw away] a lot of old things. He [used up|use up] all his boxes and [tired out|tire out] his old shoes. “What does this mark [stand for|stand for]?” a neighbour asked. “It stands for a new start,” Sardor smiled. They [hung out|hang out] together, and the evening [ended up|end up] at a café. “I [get along with|get along with] everyone,” he said, “and I won’t [stick out|stick out] about it.” Slowly, the week [sped up|speed up] and ended better than it began.',
       'Juma kuni u ko‘p eski narsalarni tashlab yuborishga majbur bo‘ldi. U barcha qutilarni ishlatib tugatdi va eski poyabzalini eskirtirdi. «Bu belgi nimani anglatadi?» deb so‘radi qo‘shni. «U yangi boshlanishni anglatadi», jilmaydi Sardor. Ular birga vaqt o‘tkazishdi va kech kafeda tugadi. «Men hamma bilan til topishaman, — dedi u, — va bu bilan maqtanmayman.» Asta-sekin hafta tezlashdi va boshlanganidan yaxshiroq tugadi.'],
      ['That weekend Sardor had to [call off|call off] a small party and [give away|give away] the cake. A friend [pointed out|point out] his mistake: he hadn’t invited anyone. His plan started to [fall apart|fall apart], but he said, “[Hold on|hold on]! I will [catch up with|catch up with] my work and meet you all on Sunday.”',
       'O‘sha hafta oxirida Sardor kichik ziyofatni bekor qilishga va tortni hadya qilishga majbur bo‘ldi. Do‘sti xatosini ko‘rsatdi: u hech kimni taklif qilmagan edi. Uning rejasi barbod bo‘la boshladi, lekin u dedi: «Kuting! Ishimga yetib olaman va yakshanba kuni hammangiz bilan uchrashaman.»']
    ],
    q: [
      ['What happened on Tuesday?', ['The dinner plan fell through.', 'He got promoted.', 'He travelled.'], 0],
      ['Why did Sardor have to deal with two projects?', ['A colleague didn’t turn up.', 'He wanted more work.', 'The boss asked.'], 0],
      ['Who did he run into?', ['His old teacher', 'His boss', 'A stranger'], 0],
      ['What did he decide to set up?', ['A small company', 'A school', 'A club'], 0],
      ['How did the week end?', ['Better than it began', 'Worse', 'Unchanged'], 0]
    ]
  }],
